# Holdr settings for `npm run start:local` and the `npm run holdr-*` commands that open your data
# folder (holdr-user, holdr-backup and the importers such as holdr-checking, holdr-retail and holdr-metals).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the same folder and uncomment what you need:
#   Windows (PowerShell):  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#   macOS (zsh):           cp .env.example .env
# Variables already set in your environment win over this file. Nothing else reads it: not the demo (`npm run demo`
# uses only its own settings), not `npm run dev` (it uses the environment only), not the offline converters
# (holdr-card-import, holdr-*-convert), and not the card sync agent or the MCP server (`npm run agent`, `npm run mcp`,
# which take options or environment variables). Never commit `.env`, and never put passwords or tokens in it.

# Where your data lives: an absolute path. Default: your per-user data folder,
#   Windows %LOCALAPPDATA%\Holdr\data, macOS ~/Library/Application Support/Holdr/data, Linux ~/.local/share/holdr/data.
# HOLDR_DATA_DIR=C:\Users\you\HoldrData
# HOLDR_DATA_DIR=/Users/you/HoldrData

# The API's port on 127.0.0.1 (default 4000). The web app's is `npm run start:local -- --web-port N` (default 5173).
# PORT=4000

# The private HTTPS address your other devices open through Tailscale Serve (docs/getting-started.md, step 6).
# HOLDR_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net

# Market data (public quotes and price history for the symbols you hold; never account data):
# Portfolio snapshots every 5 minutes for the 1-day chart: on by default; 0 turns them off.
# SNAPSHOTS_ENABLED=0
# Intraday prices for the 1-day and 1-week charts: on by default; 0 turns them off.
# HOLDR_INTRADAY_PRICES=0
# Gold and silver spot prices for the Gold page: off by default; 1 turns them on.
# HOLDR_METALS_PRICES=1
# Where prices come from: live (the default) asks the public providers above; stored answers from the daily closes
# already in the database and asks none (what the demo uses). Any other value stops Holdr.
# HOLDR_MARKET_DATA=stored

# More browser origins allowed to make changes, comma-separated. start:local always allows its own web address.
# WEB_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:5200,http://localhost:5200

# The hardened macOS deployment does not use this file: it reads holdr.conf (docs/deployment.md).
